      },
      "displayName": "Demian Katz",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Thank you, ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
           "text": "@Danny Bernstein"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " , for putting my documentation into the wiki at ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Messaging#Messaging-SetupFedoratoTalktoExternalActiveMQ"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": " – I have reviewed it and made a couple of further edits: adding a contextualizing introduction to the section, and noting some points where there might be choices to make about file paths, ports, etc., since this documentation reflects Villanova’s setup.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "If nobody has concerns about my latest revision in the wiki, I think this can be resolved (and feel free to edit my text if you can improve it!).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
