       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Bernstein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I reviewed the messaging documentation (<a href=\"https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Messaging\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Messaging</a>) so queue and topic configuration info is highlighted.  I also moved the sections around, pushing the camel stuff to the bottom and adding some links to related resources to the first sections.  Additionlly I removed the information on Karaf as we’re no longer recommending it.</p>",
     "created": "22/Sep/22 1:12 PM",
     "id": "22704",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/13719/comment/22704",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Bernstein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "22/Sep/22 1:13 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Demian Katz",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>On today’s Dev call, we talked about adding a section about setting up an external ActiveMQ and forwarding messages from Fedora. One of the advantages of this is gaining access to the web console, which is currently included by default in ActiveMQ 5.x. I’m attaching an “ActiveMQ Notes.docx” file which I assembled while setting this up in my local environment for testing. It might be adaptable into an example on the wiki – feel free to use it however you like. Details on the web console are available at <a href=\"https://activemq.apache.org/web-console\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://activemq.apache.org/web-console</a> – I didn’t have to do anything extra to set that up, I just opened an SSL tunnel to port 8161 and was immediately able to log in with the default credentials. (Obviously best practice would be to change those&#33; 🙂).</p>",
     "created": "22/Sep/22 3:24 PM",
     "id": "22705",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/13719/comment/22705",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Demian Katz",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "22/Sep/22 3:24 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/DK-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Demian Katz",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5db386745304a60c3a769d36",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Thank you, <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" data-account-id=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" accountid=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Danny Bernstein</a> , for putting my documentation into the wiki at <a href=\"https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Messaging#Messaging-SetupFedoratoTalktoExternalActiveMQ\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Messaging#Messaging-SetupFedoratoTalktoExternalActiveMQ</a> – I have reviewed it and made a couple of further edits: adding a contextualizing introduction to the section, and noting some points where there might be choices to make about file paths, ports, etc., since this documentation reflects Villanova’s setup.</p>\n\n<p>If nobody has concerns about my latest revision in the wiki, I think this can be resolved (and feel free to edit my text if you can improve it!).</p>",
     "created": "03/Nov/22 1:04 PM",
     "id": "22750",
     "jsdPublic": true,
